{"availability":"available","full":"pimterry/loglevel","name":"loglevel","description":":ledger: Minimal lightweight logging for JavaScript, adding reliable log level methods to wrap any available console.log methods","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":2746,"forks":160,"created":"2013-03-23T20:35:58Z","updated":"2025-03-20T15:13:43Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["javascript","lightweight","logging","loglevel","setlevel","stack-traces"],"demo":null,"color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T06:51:30.926Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T06:51:30.926Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T06:51:30.926Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T08:37:36.140Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T21:18:27.127Z","stars":2747,"forks":160},{"at":"2026-10-04T06:51:30.926Z","stars":2746,"forks":160}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Don't debug with logs alone - check out HTTP Toolkit: beautiful, powerful & open-source tools for building, testing & debugging HTTP(S)","Minimal lightweight simple logging for JavaScript (browsers, node.js or elsewhere). loglevel extends console.log() & friends with level-based logging and filtering, with none of console's downsides.","Loglevel is a barebones reliable everyday logging library. It does not do fancy things, it does not let you reconfigure appenders or add complex log filtering rules or boil tea (more's the pity), but it does have the all core functionality that you actually use:"],"features":["Log things at a given level (trace/debug/info/warn/error) to the console object (as seen in all modern browsers & node.js).","Filter logging by level (all the above or 'silent'), so you can disable all but error logging in production, and then run log.setLevel(\"trace\") in your console to turn it all back on for a furious debugging session.","Single file, no dependencies, weighs in at 1.4 KB minified and gzipped.","Log methods gracefully fall back to simpler console logging methods if more specific ones aren't available: so calls to log.debug() go to console.debug() if possible, or console.log() if not.","Logging calls still succeed even if there's no console object at all, so your site doesn't break when people visit with old browsers that don't support the console object (here's looking at you, IE) and similar."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/pimterry/loglevel/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"59b15c88ea89f05f98a9748c43f138f7f3b5ebf12516937a2524a01d60cda3eb","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T05:59:21.177Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T06:13:14.809Z","overviewRepoUpdated":"2025-03-20T15:13:43Z","enrichmentAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T07:14:51.784Z","latestRelease":{"name":"v1.9.2","tag":"v1.9.2","publishedAt":"2024-09-06T15:14:08Z","url":"https://github.com/pimterry/loglevel/releases/tag/v1.9.2"},"releaseCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T07:14:51.784Z","screenshots":[],"overviewAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T06:13:11.488Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Don't debug with logs alone - check out HTTP Toolkit: beautiful, powerful & open-source tools for building, testing & debugging HTTP(S)","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/pimterry/loglevel/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"59b15c88ea89f05f98a9748c43f138f7f3b5ebf12516937a2524a01d60cda3eb","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/pimterry/loglevel/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T06:13:14.809Z"},"readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/pimterry/loglevel/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T06:13:14.810Z","hash":"59b15c88ea89f05f98a9748c43f138f7f3b5ebf12516937a2524a01d60cda3eb","originalBytes":25341,"storedBytes":25341,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["log","loglevel","logging","level","logger","console","available","methods","trace","root","e.g.","message","module","version","loggers","object","run","var","add","default","error","javascript","method","when","fix","npm","plugin","set","using","log.warn",